# Custom git merge drivers — INFRA-310
#
# Drivers are registered in .git/config by scripts/setup/install-merge-drivers.sh.
# That installer is auto-run by scripts/setup/install-hooks.sh, so a fresh
# checkout / linked worktree gets them after the first hook installation.

# INFRA-8193: .chump/state.sql is no longer tracked (state.db is the only
# truth), so the chump-state-sql-regen merge driver (INFRA-310/367) is gone.

# .github/workflows/ci.yml collects append-only step additions. The ci-yml-add-row driver
# merges concurrent additions by unioning the new steps without requiring manual resolution.
.github/workflows/ci.yml merge=ci-yml-add-row

# scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit collects append-only guard blocks. The pre-commit-add-guard
# driver merges new guards by safely combining them without manual resolution.
scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit merge=pre-commit-add-guard

# Per-file gap YAMLs (docs/gaps/*.yaml) typically don't conflict (separate files per gap).
# When they do (concurrent closes on the same gap), use gap-yaml-add-line driver to
# resolve by taking ours (the current/newer state).
docs/gaps/*.yaml merge=gap-yaml-add-line

# INFRA-949: append-only YAML registries with daily conflict pattern.
#
# Both files accept ADDITIVE contributions from many PRs simultaneously
# (new ambient event kinds in EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml, new tier-2/3 env var
# names in env-vars-internal.txt). Without a merge driver, two PRs that
# each add a new entry produce textual conflicts even though the changes
# don't actually conflict semantically.
#
# `merge=union` resolves to the `union` driver registered by
# scripts/setup/install-merge-drivers.sh (scripts/git/merge-driver-union.sh),
# which keeps both sides and is list-item aware for EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml.
# INFRA-8223: the original INFRA-1419 registration (`git merge-file -p ... > %A`)
# truncated its own input and wrote LEFT/RIGHT markers; if a checkout still has
# it, re-run `bash scripts/setup/install-merge-drivers.sh`.
#
# History: this conflict pattern bit five PRs today (#1597/#1605/#1609/
# #1648/#1670) requiring manual union-merge resolution via Python regex.
docs/observability/EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml merge=union
scripts/ci/env-vars-internal.txt merge=union

# INFRA-1201: web/v2/index.html is a PWA append-only hot file. Each new PWA
# feature (PRODUCT-NNN / INFRA-1011/1013-style) adds a <script src="X.js">
# entry to the script-loading block + (optionally) a <chump-X></chump-X>
# custom-element placement before the closing </body>. Both are append-only
# zones; concurrent feature PRs hit the same blocks and produce textual
# conflicts even though the additions don't actually overlap semantically.
#
# As of 2026-05-14 hot-file audit: 3 simultaneous PRs (#1827 INFRA-1011,
# #1860 PRODUCT-090, plus others) were stuck DIRTY for hours on this file.
#
# git's built-in `merge=union` concatenates unique lines from both sides.
# Same approach already validated for EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml + env-vars-internal.txt.
# Risk mitigation: pre-commit/duplicate-script-tag guard (INFRA-1201) catches
# the rare case where two PRs add THE SAME <script src="X.js"> independently.
web/v2/index.html merge=union

# INFRA-1389: extend merge-driver coverage to remaining hot shared files.
#
# All three files below follow the same append-only pattern: concurrent PRs
# add new entries at the end (new dep in Cargo.toml, new component class in
# app.js, new route arm in src/main.rs). The generic merge-driver-append-only.sh
# driver handles all three — pure-append check + tail deduplication + append.
#
# Dedup is important for Cargo.toml: two PRs that each independently add
# `serde = "1"` would otherwise double-register the entry.

# Cargo.toml — new [[bin]] entries, new [dependencies], new [features] lines.
Cargo.toml merge=cargo-toml-append

# web/v2/app.js — new component class definitions appended before the Router,
# new VIEWS map entries, new CHUMP_CADENCES subtab entries.
web/v2/app.js merge=js-append

# src/main.rs — REMOVED from append-only driver (2026-05-23 P0 fix).
#
# Tonight's pattern (5+ PRs across #2350 #2351 #2356 silently dropped
# mod declarations during auto-rebase): the append-only driver assumes
# both sides are pure appends. main.rs gets internal edits regularly
# (bug fixes, dispatch refactors), which fails the pure-append check.
# When the driver falls back to standard 3-way merge, line content near
# the conflict boundary gets silently dropped instead of producing
# conflict markers.
#
# Removing the merge=rust-main-append attribute restores standard
# 3-way merge for main.rs — produces clear conflict markers when the
# operator needs to resolve, instead of silent data loss.
#
# Real fix: INFRA-1687 / INFRA-1748 (decompose main.rs into
# inventory-style self-registration; kills the hot-file class entirely).
# Until that lands, plain 3-way merge is the lesser evil.

# RESILIENT-344: extend built-in merge=union to the remaining append-only CI
# registries/allowlists. Same append-only pattern as env-vars-internal.txt /
# EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml above: many PRs concurrently append one line each. Without
# a union driver those textual conflicts SURVIVE a rebase and re-DIRTY green PRs
# on every subsequent merge — the green-then-reconflict spiral (2026-08-15 fleet
# incident: PRs went green, re-conflicted on event-registry-reserved.txt, rebased,
# re-ran 15-20min CI, and another merge re-conflicted them → never landed).
# All are flat line-lists (one reserved-id / allowlisted-name per line); git core
# `union` concatenates unique lines from both sides — no custom driver, no install
# step (unlike the INFRA-310 custom drivers that need install-merge-drivers.sh).
scripts/ci/event-registry-reserved.txt merge=union
scripts/ci/ambient-emit-allowlist.txt merge=union
scripts/ci/bypass-env-var-allowlist.txt merge=union
scripts/ci/coord-shell-allowlist.txt merge=union
scripts/ci/cross-pr-allowlist.txt merge=union
scripts/ci/legacy-bypass-trailer-allowlist.txt merge=union
scripts/ci/raw-gh-allowlist.txt merge=union
scripts/ci/research-integrity-phantom-allowlist.txt merge=union
scripts/ci/shell-test-allowlist.txt merge=union

# ── INFRA-1688: extend union to the append-only hot files that still reap PRs ──
# Proven 2026-08-22: rebasing keystone PRs (Race Control #4096, coherence #4095)
# onto main conflicted ONLY on these append-only registries — the union-marked
# files auto-merged cleanly. Each is one-entry-per-line; union concatenates unique
# lines from both sides, dissolving the append-collision that sends good PRs
# CONFLICTING → reaped. Same rationale as INFRA-310 / RESILIENT-344 above.
scripts/ops/organ-manifest.txt merge=union
scripts/setup/optional-installers-allowlist.txt merge=union
scripts/ci/preflight-ci-parity-exceptions.txt merge=union

# RESILIENT-1544: union-merge the preflight overflow list so parallel PR appends never conflict
scripts/ci/preflight-extra-test-scripts.txt merge=union
